r-rail on the 0.139 CLI surface. The binary-SHA pin\n# (codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt -> d3be844c...) remains the real supply-chain\n# gate; this semver range is the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message. Per\n# ADR-111 the 0.128->0.139 jump runs the locked-corpus catch_rate check\n# (Owner elected to RUN it this ceremony, not defer) — see PLAN-142 §4.\n#\n# PLAN-156 update (S269 2026-07-12, SENT-CX-PIN): widened upper bound to\n# <0.145.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.144.1 is in-range — the\n# bump that restores frontier-model access (GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna are\n# first-class from 0.143.0; 0.139 cannot run them). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED\n# at >=0.128.0 (debate C10 / pair-rail R2: raising it would drop an\n# in-flight RC verdict out of range in release.yml step-15 and red-lock a\n# GA cut — widen-upper-only is the ONLY safe shape during any release\n# window; this bump was executed OUTSIDE an open release window).\n# Empirical base: PLAN-156/artifacts/characterization-grok-codex-S269.md\n# (0.144.1 flag surface verified — the 0.139 verified-compose\n# `exec --color never --sandbox <mode> -o <file> --output-schema --json -m`\n# is UNCHANGED; sandbox enum still read-only|workspace-write|\n# danger-full-access; reasoning-effort accepts max/xhigh client-side;\n# 0.144.0 open bugs #31873/#31860/#31826 triaged non-blocking, #31869\n# CLOSED upstream 2026-07-10). Locked-corpus catch_rate check: Owner\n# elects run-vs-defer at SENT-CX-PIN signing (S246 precedent: run it).\n#\n# PLAN-174 update (S318 2026-08-20, pack SENT-S318): widened upper bound to\n# <0.148.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.147.0 is in-range — the bump\n# that unblocks the PLAN-174 W2 wire (the pair-rail rounds since S317 already\n# ran on the 0.147.0 binary, advisory). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0\n# (same widen-upper-only shape as S269: executed OUTSIDE any open release\n# window — GA v1.3.0 was cut 2026-08-17 and no rc is in flight). The ADR-182\n# payload manifest (codex-cli-pin-manifest.json, re-pinned in this same pack:\n# payload sha256 19c4f144... for 0.147.0/aarch64-apple-darwin, npm_integrity\n# recorded from the platform artifact) remains the real supply-chain gate;\n# this semver range stays the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message.\n# Locked-corpus catch_rate check (ADR-111 §2): Owner elects run-vs-defer at\n# pack signing, recorded in the SENT-S318 sentinel Scope.\n\n# PLAN-189 update (S352 2026-09-15): widened upper bound to <0.155.0 so the\n# Owner's installed codex-cli 0.154.0 is in-range. The rail was pinned at\n# 0.147.0 while the global CLI had moved SEVEN releases ahead, so every rail\n# round ran on a revisor older than the one the Owner uses interactively.\n# Per ADR-111 §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase\n# 4-bis re-run: no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED\n# CONSEQUENCE: this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken before\n# and after this commit are NOT comparable (S352 rule: re-test on a new\n# generation, instrument intact). The 93/93/91 validity series measured in\n# S352 was taken under 0.147.0.\n\n# PLAN-189 update (S356 2026-09-18, pack codex-pin-0155): widened upper bound\n# to <0.156.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.155.0 is in-range. 0.155.0\n# was published to npm on 2026-09-17; with the ADR-182 exact-version payload\n# manifest the pair-rail went fail-CLOSED in this repo (`--verify-codex-pin`\n# -> mismatch payload_sha256_mismatch) until this re-pin. LOWER BOUND\n# UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape), executed\n# OUTSIDE any open release window: GA v1.4.0 was cut 2026-09-15 and\n# v1.4.1-rc.1 is cut only AFTER this commit. Per ADR-111\n# §pin-update-protocol this widening does NOT trigger a Phase 4-bis re-run:\n# no new locked-corpus measurement has been taken. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE\n# (same as S352): this changes the INSTRUMENT — rail measurements taken\n# before and after this commit are NOT comparable. The payload manifest\n#