{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WEAhCdv4teHkxRPYRRA2P7","type":"tool_result","content":"17\t\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n21\t# ADR-163 Amendment (PLAN-169 S328) — runner-normalized SECOND KEY\n22\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n23\t#\n24\t# Evidence: `check_output_secrets` measured p95 361.4 / 424.8 / 229.1 ms on\n25\t# ubuntu-latest against the 180 ms hard ceiling while the ADR-163 contention\n26\t# pre-probe (`python3 -c pass`, the SPAWN floor) read UNCONTENDED at 7.76 ms\n27\t# and the same hook bytes measured 70-77 ms locally — and the immediately\n28\t# preceding commit PASSED 3.5 h earlier with ZERO files touched under the\n29\t# hook tree. `python3 -c pass` prices process CREATION; it is structurally\n30\t# blind to a runner that is slow-but-uncontended once execution starts.\n31\t#\n32\t# Cure: a SECOND key, relative, against an EXECUTION reference measured in\n33\t# the same run, round-robin-interleaved with the hook samples so both keys\n34\t# price the same scheduler window. The absolute ceiling STAYS (no third\n35\t# recalibration — \"bump the number\" already failed at ADR-163:291).\n36\t#\n37\t# PHASE 1 (this landing): labels are computed and PUBLISHED; exit codes stay\n38\t# byte-identical to today. K is not derivable — zero paired (hook, ref)\n39\t# samples exist anywhere. Phase 2 pins K_e per entry from an advisory window\n40\t# and is plumbed here (`--relative-k-source`) but INERT without that file.\n41\t\n42\t# Closed set, DERIVED by every consumer (never recalled — the\n43\t# `feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled` class).\n44\t_OUTCOME_LABELS: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n45\t    \"pass\",\n46\t    \"advisory_slow_runner\",\n47\t    \"real_regression\",\n48\t    \"infrastructure_contended\",\n49\t)\n50\t\n51\t# label -> process exit code, PHASE 2 only. Phase 1 keeps today's 0/1.\n52\t_LABEL_EXIT_CLASS: Dict[str, int] = {\n53\t    \"pass\": 0,\n54\t    \"advisory_slow_runner\": 0,\n55\t    \"real_regression\": 1,\n56\t    \"infrastructure_contended\": 5,\n57\t}\n58\t\n59\t# Aggregation precedence (strongest verdict first): a PROVEN regression on\n60\t# any entry outranks contention elsewhere, and contention outranks amnesty.\n61\t_LABEL_PRECEDENCE: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n62\t    \"real_regression\",\n63\t    \"infrastructure_contended\",\n64\t    \"advisory_slow_runner\",\n65\t    \"pass\",\n66\t)\n67\t\n68\t# The COMPLETE set of report keys the second key may add. Declared here so\n69\t# the back-compat test can assert `set(new_report) - set(old_report)` is a\n70\t# subset of it: a future key added without registering it here turns that\n71\t# test RED instead of silently widening the report.\n72\t_SECOND_KEY_REPORT_KEYS: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n73\t    \"phase\",\n74\t    \"verdict_label\",\n75\t    \"exit_class\",\n76\t    \"outcome_labels\",\n77\t    \"exec_reference\",\n78\t    \"relative_advisory\",\n79\t    \"strict_relative\",\n80\t    \"abs_backstop_ms\",\n81\t    \"ref_drift_max\",\n82\t    \"wall_budget_seconds\",\n83\t    \"wall_deadline_seconds\",\n84\t    \"wall_exceeded\",\n85\t    \"elapsed_seconds\",\n86\t    \"relative_warnings\",\n87\t    \"ref_source_sha256\",\n88\t    \"ref_samples_per_entry\",\n89\t    \"relative_note\",\n90\t)\n91\t_SECOND_KEY_ENTRY_KEYS: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n92\t    \"ref_p50_ms\",\n93\t    \"ref_p95_ms\",\n94\t    \"ref_samples\",\n95\t    \"ref_split_half_drift\",\n96\t    \"ref_valid\",\n97\t    \"ref_failed\",\n98\t    \"R_e\",\n99\t    \"K_e\",\n100\t    \"rel_ok\",\n101\t    \"verdict_label\",\n102\t    \"phase\",\n103\t)\n104\t\n105\t# Absolute backstop above which a slow runner still FAILS instead of being\n106\t# granted amnesty. OPEN QUESTION for the Owner: this number has no evidence\n107\t# behind it — it is a \"what latency is unusable in a real session\" judgment.\n108\t_ABS_BACKSTOP_MS = 600.0\n109\t\n110\t# Reference samples per corpus entry (round-robin). The relative key gates on\n111\t# p50, where the ADR-163 nearest-rank index collapse cannot arise, so the\n112\t# n>=22 separation rule does not bind here; 40 is the adopted floor.\n113\t_REF_SAMPLES_PER_ENTRY = 40\n114\t\n115\t# Split-half p50 drift above which the REFERENCE itself is untrustworthy:\n116\t# the machine moved mid-entry, so the ratio prices two different machines.\n117\t_REF_DRIFT_MAX = 1.5\n118\t\n119\t# Self-cap fraction of --wall-budget-seconds. The cap fires BEFORE the\n120\t# workflow's `timeout 420`, so rc 124 becomes unreachable in practice.\n121\t_WALL_BUDGET_SAFETY_FRACTION = 0.9\n122\t# (rail round-1 P2 retired `_WALL_CHECK_EVERY`: the wall is checked on EVERY\n123\t# iteration and again before the reference lane, so there is no stride to\n124\t# name. A stride here is a defect, not a tuning knob — it made the 378s\n125\t# self-cap miss by up to ~300s, which is the rc124 the cap exists to avoid.)\n126\t\n127\t# --- the frozen execution reference ----------------------------------------\n128\t# Three terms, source-pinned by sha256 in the report. Any edit changes that\n129\t# hash DELIBERATELY: a heavier reference silently LOOSENS the relative key.\n130\t_REF_EXEC_SOURCE = r'''#!/usr/bin/env python3\n131\t# Frozen EXECUTION reference — ADR-163 Amendment (PLAN-169 S328).\n132\t#\n133\t# THREE TERMS, in order:\n134\t#   1. cold stdlib imports (json / re / hashlib / pathlib) + a fixed\n135\t#      re.compile set   -- prices the interpreter + import machinery;\n136\t#   2. a fixed CPU-bound hashing loop        -- prices the core;\n137\t#   3. M x open/append/flock/fsync/rename    -- prices the filesystem.\n138\t#\n139\t# HARD CONTRACT: stdlib ONLY, and NOTHING from the framework's own hook\n140\t# tree. The regression class this gate exists to catch IS an eager\n141\t# framework import; a reference paying that same import would inflate\n142\t# numerator AND denominator and go blind to its own reason to exist. An\n143\t# anti-coupling test walks this source's AST and asserts it.\n144\timport os\n145\timport sys\n146\t\n147\ttry:\n148\t    import fcntl as _locker\n149\texcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover - non-POSIX\n150\t    _locker = None\n151\t\n152\t# Term sizing is MEASURED, not guessed (local macOS, 2026-08-25, N=30):\n153\t# spawn floor 23.9ms; imports +6.4ms; these constants add ~+16ms of CPU and\n154\t# ~+5ms of locked IO, putting the reference at p50 ~46ms of which ~48% is\n155\t# EXECUTION. The first draft (4000/6) sat at 34ms / 30% execution — barely\n156\t# more than the spawn probe it replaces, which would leave the ratio nearly"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"613e580a-b626-4aa0-966c-6b7a50b955be","uuid":"5ccc6202-00f5-41f4-9668-0b7c060b4713","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:40:57.028Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_profile_opus_parts/reference.py","content":"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ADR-163 Amendment (PLAN-169 S328) — runner-normalized SECOND KEY\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n#\n# Evidence: `check_output_secrets` measured p95 361.4 / 424.8 / 229.1 ms on\n# ubuntu-latest against the 180 ms hard ceiling while the ADR-163 contention\n# pre-probe (`python3 -c pass`, the SPAWN floor) read UNCONTENDED at 7.76 ms\n# and the same hook bytes measured 70-77 ms locally — and the immediately\n# preceding commit PASSED 3.5 h earlier with ZERO files touched under the\n# hook tree. `python3 -c pass` prices process CREATION; it is structurally\n# blind to a runner that is slow-but-uncontended once execution starts.\n#\n# Cure: a SECOND key, relative, against an EXECUTION reference measured in\n# the same run, round-robin-interleaved with the hook samples so both keys\n# price the same scheduler window. The absolute ceiling STAYS (no third\n# recalibration — \"bump the number\" already failed at ADR-163:291).\n#\n# PHASE 1 (this landing): labels are computed and PUBLISHED; exit codes stay\n# byte-identical to today. K is not derivable — zero paired (hook, ref)\n# samples exist anywhere. Phase 2 pins K_e per entry from an advisory window\n# and is plumbed here (`--relative-k-source`) but INERT without that file.\n\n# Closed set, DERIVED by every consumer (never recalled — the\n# `feedback-closed-sets-must-be-derived-not-recalled` class).\n_OUTCOME_LABELS: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"pass\",\n    \"advisory_slow_runner\",\n    \"real_regression\",\n    \"infrastructure_contended\",\n)\n\n# label -> process exit code, PHASE 2 only. Phase 1 keeps today's 0/1.\n_LABEL_EXIT_CLASS: Dict[str, int] = {\n    \"pass\": 0,\n    \"advisory_slow_runner\": 0,\n    \"real_regression\": 1,\n    \"infrastructure_contended\": 5,\n}\n\n# Aggregation precedence (strongest verdict first): a PROVEN regression on\n# any entry outranks contention elsewhere, and contention outranks amnesty.\n_LABEL_PRECEDENCE: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"real_regression\",\n    \"infrastructure_contended\",\n    \"advisory_slow_runner\",\n    \"pass\",\n)\n\n# The COMPLETE set of report keys the second key may add. Declared here so\n# the back-compat test can assert `set(new_report) - set(old_report)` is a\n# subset of it: a future key added without registering it here turns that\n# test RED instead of silently widening the report.\n_SECOND_KEY_REPORT_KEYS: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"phase\",\n    \"verdict_label\",\n    \"exit_class\",\n    \"outcome_labels\",\n    \"exec_reference\",\n    \"relative_advisory\",\n    \"strict_relative\",\n    \"abs_backstop_ms\",\n    \"ref_drift_max\",\n    \"wall_budget_seconds\",\n    \"wall_deadline_seconds\",\n    \"wall_exceeded\",\n    \"elapsed_seconds\",\n    \"relative_warnings\",\n    \"ref_source_sha256\",\n    \"ref_samples_per_entry\",\n    \"relative_note\",\n)\n_SECOND_KEY_ENTRY_KEYS: Tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"ref_p50_ms\",\n    \"ref_p95_ms\",\n    \"ref_samples\",\n    \"ref_split_half_drift\",\n    \"ref_valid\",\n    \"ref_failed\",\n    \"R_e\",\n    \"K_e\",\n    \"rel_ok\",\n    \"verdict_label\",\n    \"phase\",\n)\n\n# Absolute backstop above which a slow runner still FAILS instead of being\n# granted amnesty. OPEN QUESTION for the Owner: this number has no evidence\n# behind it — it is a \"what latency is unusable in a real session\" judgment.\n_ABS_BACKSTOP_MS = 600.0\n\n# Reference samples per corpus entry (round-robin). The relative key gates on\n# p50, where the ADR-163 nearest-rank index collapse cannot arise, so the\n# n>=22 separation rule does not bind here; 40 is the adopted floor.\n_REF_SAMPLES_PER_ENTRY = 40\n\n# Split-half p50 drift above which the REFERENCE itself is untrustworthy:\n# the machine moved mid-entry, so the ratio prices two different machines.\n_REF_DRIFT_MAX = 1.5\n\n# Self-cap fraction of --wall-budget-seconds. The cap fires BEFORE the\n# workflow's `timeout 420`, so rc 124 becomes unreachable in practice.\n_WALL_BUDGET_SAFETY_FRACTION = 0.9\n# (rail round-1 P2 retired `_WALL_CHECK_EVERY`: the wall is checked on EVERY\n# iteration and again before the reference lane, so there is no stride to\n# name. A stride here is a defect, not a tuning knob — it made the 378s\n# self-cap miss by up to ~300s, which is the rc124 the cap exists to avoid.)\n\n# --- the frozen execution reference ----------------------------------------\n# Three terms, source-pinned by sha256 in the report. Any edit changes that\n# hash DELIBERATELY: a heavier reference silently LOOSENS the relative key.\n_REF_EXEC_SOURCE = r'''#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Frozen EXECUTION reference — ADR-163 Amendment (PLAN-169 S328).\n#\n# THREE TERMS, in order:\n#   1. cold stdlib imports (json / re / hashlib / pathlib) + a fixed\n#      re.compile set   -- prices the interpreter + import machinery;\n#   2. a fixed CPU-bound hashing loop        -- prices the core;\n#   3. M x open/append/flock/fsync/rename    -- prices the filesystem.\n#\n# HARD CONTRACT: stdlib ONLY, and NOTHING from the framework's own hook\n# tree. The regression class this gate exists to catch IS an eager\n# framework import; a reference paying that same import would inflate\n# numerator AND denominator and go blind to its own reason to exist. An\n# anti-coupling test walks this source's AST and asserts it.\nimport os\nimport sys\n\ntry:\n    import fcntl as _locker\nexcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover - non-POSIX\n    _locker = None\n\n# Term sizing is MEASURED, not guessed (local macOS, 2026-08-25, N=30):\n# spawn floor 23.9ms; imports +6.4ms; these constants add ~+16ms of CPU and\n# ~+5ms of locked IO, putting the reference at p50 ~46ms of which ~48% is\n# EXECUTION. The first draft (4000/6) sat at 34ms / 30% execution — barely\n# more than the spawn probe it replaces, which would leave the ratio nearly","numLines":140,"startLine":17,"totalLines":460}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WEAhCdv4teHkxRPYRRA2P7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
