ackage exits 1 with a traceback, not the documented \"2 = detector internal error\".\n- Minimal fix: move the import and the install() call inside that try.\n\nP2-5. .claude/hooks/_lib/_profile_opus_parts/latency.py:119-127 (carried, moved word for word, not introduced by this delta)\n- Scenario: the isolation scrub drops CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE but not CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH, and CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH outranks CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR (_audit_log_parts/paths_skills.py:10).\n- A maintainer who runs --hook-latency with CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH exported appends about 1,000 or more measured hook rows to the live HMAC chain. That breaks the docstring promise \"never the real ~/.claude\" and is the same class as the diagnose-output-hook P1 cured in v1.4.3-rc.1.\n- Minimal fix: add CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH and the other location variables that diagnose-output-hook.py strips to the scrub tuple.\n\nP2-6. Housekeeping\n- .github/CODEOWNERS:122 still names only .claude/scripts/profile-opus-4-7.py. Its logic now lives in .claude/hooks/_lib/_profile_opus_parts/; add an entry if per-file ownership is intended.\n- The night-mode.py:320-324 header comment (\"Path resolution — anchored in FUNCTIONS\") now introduces an import block; update it.","decision":"GO","sentence":"In this payload the four script splits keep behavior and the fail direction intact, the parts ship to installs, condition 7 and the pin facts behind condition 9 hold against the code, and what I found is P2 only: the re-pin generator mislabels a floor-to-bounded change as a widening, and there are minor gaps in exit-code contracts and isolation."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2275,"cache_read_input_tokens":255990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2275},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[]